er no if references are tags or aliases, or no rollback procedure exists.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** No rollback procedure, recovery setup or model retirement date appears in this repo\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## C07.2\n\n**Check:** Credentials and permission grants are managed apart from the rolled-back artifacts, so a rollback does not restore revoked access.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open the rollback procedure. 2) Check what it restores. 3) Answer no if it re-applies IAM policies, RoleBindings, secrets, or API keys from the old release, so revoked access comes back. Answer unknown if credentials are managed in another system and the repo does not show how.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** No rollback procedure, recovery setup or model retirement date appears in this repo\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## C07.3\n\n**Check:** The rollback procedure handles memory and index state, checkpoints, and queued work explicitly (drain, migrate, or discard), so unsafe side effects are not replayed.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open the rollback procedure. 2) Look for explicit steps for memory and index state, checkpoints, and queued work: drain, migrate, or discard. 3) Answer no if any of these is not handled, or queued work is replayed as-is.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** No rollback procedure, recovery setup or model retirement date appears in this repo\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## C07.4\n\n**Check:** Each hosted model named in the recovery setup has a recorded retirement date.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) List the hosted models named in the recovery setup. 2) Check each has a recorded retirement date. 3) Answer no if any hosted model lacks one.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** No rollback procedure, recovery setup or model retirement date appears in this repo\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to C07.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in ve